{"name":"Peace Yellow","hex":"#eecf9e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of tranquility, quiet, and harmony. For instance, a state free from civil disturbance.","A feeling of tranquility, free from oppressive and unpleasant thoughts and emotions."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Shut up!, silence!; be quiet, be silent.","Peace out; goodbye."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peace"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peace","blocks":[{"text":"Peace is a state of harmony in the absence of hostility and violence. In a societal sense, peace is commonly used to mean a lack of conflict and freedom from fear of violence between individuals or groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Peace_dove_%283329620077%29.jpg/330px-Peace_dove_%283329620077%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace","wikidata":"Q454"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Eir%C3%A9n%C3%A9_et_Ploutos.JPG/330px-Eir%C3%A9n%C3%A9_et_Ploutos.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Eir%C3%A9n%C3%A9_et_Ploutos.JPG/330px-Eir%C3%A9n%C3%A9_et_Ploutos.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Statue of Eirene, goddess of peace in ancient Greek religion, with the infant Plutus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEir%C3%A9n%C3%A9_et_Ploutos.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Beowulf_-_frithu_sibb.jpg/250px-Beowulf_-_frithu_sibb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/Beowulf_-_frithu_sibb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Beowulf_-_frithu_sibb.jpg/250px-Beowulf_-_frithu_sibb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Before the word 'peace' came into English lexicon, Anglo-Saxons used a phrase \"friðu sibb\" for \"pledge of peace\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeowulf_-_f